# 1. Purpose

This document specifies the local development environment for the OPEX Budgeting System (OBS) on macOS. It defines the required toolchain, the local substitutes for cloud services (Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Server, Azure Blob Storage, Microsoft Entra ID), the repository structure, the process for running the full stack locally, and the local testing strategy. It is intended for consumption by Claude Code and any developer working on the OBS implementation.

This specification supplements the Build Sequencing Plan v1.1. Every phase in that plan must be buildable, runnable, and testable using the local environment defined here, without requiring a live connection to Azure, PostgreSQL Flexible Server, or Microsoft Entra ID.

# 2. Local Environment Design Decisions

| **Decision** | **Choice** | **Rationale** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **PostgreSQL substitute** | DuckDB (local file-based) | DuckDB supports SQL, is embeddable in Python, and requires no server process. It is a self-contained analogue to Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Server for development purposes. All obs.* table schemas are mirrored exactly. |
| **Entra ID substitute** | Local mock auth middleware | A dev-only FastAPI middleware injects a configurable test user identity, bypassing all OIDC/OAuth flows. The middleware is activated by environment variable LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS=true and must never be enabled outside the local environment. |
| **Azure Blob Storage substitute** | Local filesystem directory | A designated local directory (/local-data/landing-zone/) substitutes for the Azure Blob Storage landing zone. The ingestion pipeline detects its target path via environment variable and works identically against the local directory. |
| **Azure Functions substitute** | Python scripts invoked manually or via Makefile | Ingestion pipeline jobs are plain Python scripts that can be run manually or via make commands. No host-specific runtime dependencies exist in the pipeline code per the hosting-agnostic requirement. |
| **Microsoft Teams / Email alerts** | Console log only (local) | Pipeline alert notifications print to the console in local mode. The notification channel is toggled by environment variable ALERT_CHANNEL=console│teams│email. |
| **Frontend proxy** | Vite dev server proxy | The Vite development server proxies /api/* requests to the local FastAPI instance, eliminating CORS issues during local development. |
| **Secret management** | Local .env files (git-ignored) | Azure Key Vault is not used locally. All secrets and configuration values are stored in .env files that are explicitly excluded from version control. |

# 3. Prerequisites — macOS Toolchain

Install the following tools before beginning. All version constraints are minimums unless a specific version is required.

## 3.1 Core Runtime Dependencies

| **Tool** | **Minimum Version** | **Installation** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Homebrew** | Latest | https://brew.sh — macOS package manager. Install first; all other tools are installed via Homebrew or it manages their version managers. |
| **Python** | 3.11 | brew install pyenv, then pyenv install 3.11 and pyenv global 3.11. Do not use the macOS system Python. |
| **Node.js** | 20 LTS | brew install nvm, then nvm install 20 and nvm use 20. Do not use a globally installed Node.js. |
