# 5. Environment Variables

Copy .env.local.example to .env.local and populate the values. The .env.local file is loaded by python-dotenv in the backend and by Vite in the frontend. Never commit .env.local.

## 5.1 Backend Environment Variables (.env.local)

| **Variable** | **Local Value** | **Purpose** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS** | true | Activates the mock auth middleware. Must be false or absent in all non-local environments. |
| **LOCAL_AUTH_USER_ID** | dev-admin-001 | The user_id injected by the mock auth middleware. Must match a record in obs.users. |
| **LOCAL_AUTH_USER_EMAIL** | admin@obs.local | The email injected by the mock auth middleware. |
| **LOCAL_AUTH_USER_NAME** | Local Admin | The display name injected by the mock auth middleware. |
| **DB_ENGINE** | duckdb | Selects the database engine. duckdb for local; postgresql for production. |
| **DUCKDB_PATH** | ./local-data/obs.duckdb | Path to the local DuckDB database file. |
| **LANDING_ZONE_PATH** | ./local-data/landing-zone | Local filesystem path substituting for Azure Blob Storage landing zone. |
| **ARCHIVE_PATH** | ./local-data/archive | Local filesystem path for processed files. |
| **ERROR_PATH** | ./local-data/error | Local filesystem path for rejected files. |
| **ALERT_CHANNEL** | console | Pipeline alert channel. console for local; teams or email for production. |
| **NOTIFICATION_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS** | 60 | Notification polling interval in seconds. |
| **CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS** | http://localhost:5173 | Allowed CORS origins. Matches Vite default dev server port. |
| **LOG_LEVEL** | DEBUG | Application log level. |

## 5.2 Frontend Environment Variables (.env.local in frontend/)

| **Variable** | **Local Value** | **Purpose** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **VITE_API_BASE_URL** | http://localhost:8000 | Base URL for the backend API. The Vite proxy rewrites /api/* to this value. |
| **VITE_AUTH_ENABLED** | false | When false, the frontend skips the Entra ID OIDC login flow and treats the session as authenticated. Matches LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS on the backend. |

# 6. Local Authentication Bypass

Because Microsoft Entra ID requires a live tenant and registered application, the local environment uses a mock authentication middleware that short-circuits the entire OIDC/OAuth flow.

## 6.1 Backend Mock Auth Middleware

When LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS=true, the FastAPI dependency that normally validates an Entra ID JWT token is replaced by a function that reads the LOCAL_AUTH_USER_* environment variables and returns a synthetic CurrentUser object. The rest of the authorization pipeline — capability flag checks, cost center grant checks, confidential data enforcement — operates identically, because it receives the same CurrentUser type regardless of how the user was authenticated.

| **# backend/app/auth/middleware.py (excerpt) def get_current_user() -****>**** CurrentUser:     if settings.LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS:         return CurrentUser(             user_id=settings.LOCAL_AUTH_USER_ID,             email=settings.LOCAL_AUTH_USER_EMAIL,             display_name=settings.LOCAL_AUTH_USER_NAME,         )     # ... real Entra ID JWT validation ...** |
| --- |

| **Security: ****LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS must be implemented as a hard check against the environment variable — it must not be togglable via an API call or a request header. A startup assertion must raise an error if LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS=true and the application is not running on localhost.** |
| --- |

## 6.2 Frontend Auth Bypass

When VITE_AUTH_ENABLED=false, the frontend AuthContext skips the MSAL/OIDC redirect and immediately sets the session state to authenticated. No token is present in memory; API requests are made without an Authorization header. The backend mock middleware accepts requests with no Authorization header when LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS=true.

## 6.3 Test Users

The schema seed scripts (schema/seed/) populate obs.users with the following pre-configured local test users. Use LOCAL_AUTH_USER_ID to switch between them during development.

| **user_id** | **Role / Grants** | **Purpose** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **dev-admin-001** | is_administrator = TRUE | Full system access. Default local user. |
| **dev-costcenter-001** | ALL_WRITE standard grant + ALL_WRITE confidential on CC-1001 | Test cost center owner with confidential access. |
| **dev-readonly-001** | ALL_READ standard grant on CC-1001, ALL_NONE confidential | Test read-only user without confidential access. |
| **dev-finance-001** | is_finance_reviewer = TRUE, ALL_READ on CC-1001 | Test Finance Reviewer. |
| **dev-modeler-001** | is_system_modeler = TRUE | Test System Modeler. |
| **dev-reportdev-001** | is_report_developer = TRUE | Test Report Developer. |

# 7. Local Database — DuckDB

DuckDB serves as the local substitute for Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Server. All obs.* table schemas are defined in schema/bootstrap.sql and match the schemas specified across all OBS specifications exactly. Column names, data types, and constraints are identical to the PostgreSQL production schemas.

## 7.1 Database Abstraction Layer

The backend database access layer (backend/app/db/) uses an environment-switchable engine. When DB_ENGINE=duckdb, all queries execute against the local DuckDB file. When DB_ENGINE=postgresql, queries execute against Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Server via a direct PostgreSQL connection. No query logic changes between environments — only the connection object differs.

| **# backend/app/db/engine.py (excerpt) def get_connection():     if settings.DB_ENGINE == ****'****duckdb****'****:         return duckdb.connect(settings.DUCKDB_PATH)     elif settings.DB_ENGINE == ****'****postgresql****'****:         return psycopg2.connect(settings.PG_CONNECTION_STRING)  # production only** |
| --- |

## 7.2 Schema Bootstrap

Run the following command to create all obs.* tables in the local DuckDB database. This is idempotent — it uses CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS throughout and is safe to run multiple times.

| **make db-bootstrap # or directly: python -c ****"****import duckdb; conn = duckdb.connect(****'****./local-data/obs.duckdb****'****); conn.executemany(open(****'****schema/bootstrap.sql****'****).read()[:1])****"**** # Recommended: use the Makefile target which handles multi-statement execution correctly.** |
| --- |

## 7.3 Seed Data

After bootstrapping, load seed data to make the system immediately usable for development. Seed scripts are in schema/seed/ and are applied in dependency order by make db-seed.

| **Seed Script** | **Data Loaded** | **Required For** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **01_users.sql** | Test users (Section 6.3) into obs.users | Phase 1 onwards |
| **02_cost_center_hierarchy.sql** | Sample cost center hierarchy (3 levels, ~10 cost centers) into obs.cost_center_hierarchy_nodes | Phase 2 onwards |
| **03_account_hierarchy.sql** | Sample account hierarchy (expense accounts) into obs.expense_accounts and obs.account_hierarchy_nodes | Phase 2 onwards |
| **04_user_grants.sql** | Cost center grant assignments for test users into obs.user_cost_center_grants | Phase 1 onwards |
| **05_business_rules.sql** | Sample merit increase rate, burden rates, component mappings, overhead rates for the current fiscal year | Phase 3 onwards |
| **06_budget_versions.sql** | One draft budget version for the current fiscal year | Phase 5 onwards |
| **07_actuals.sql** | Sample actuals records for the current fiscal year YTD | Phase 2 onwards |

| **make db-seed # Applies all seed scripts in order against ./local-data/obs.duckdb** |
| --- |

## 7.4 DuckDB / PostgreSQL Compatibility Notes

DuckDB does not implement PostgreSQL B-tree / partial index tuning or PostgreSQL INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE semantics natively. The following adaptations apply in the local environment only:

- PostgreSQL INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE upserts are implemented as DELETE + INSERT pairs in DuckDB. The db/ abstraction layer provides a merge() helper that branches on DB_ENGINE.

- Append-only enforcement for the audit log is enforced in application code (no UPDATE or DELETE calls to obs.audit_log) rather than by the storage engine. An integration test verifies this.

- PostgreSQL index definitions are not applied in DuckDB — no action required locally.

- PostgreSQL retention policies are not applicable locally — the DuckDB file is the complete database.

# 8. Running the Full Stack Locally

The Makefile provides all commands needed to run the full stack. Three terminal sessions are required: one for the backend API, one for the frontend dev server, and optionally one for running pipeline scripts.

## 8.1 First-Time Setup

Run this sequence once after cloning the repository:

| **# 1. Install Python dependencies python -m venv .venv ****&****&**** source .venv/bin/activate pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -r backend/requirements-dev.txt # 2. Install Node dependencies cd frontend ****&****&**** npm install ****&****&**** cd .. # 3. Copy and configure environment variables cp .env.local.example .env.local cp frontend/.env.local.example frontend/.env.local # Edit both files as needed — defaults work for most local development # 4. Create local data directories make dirs # Creates: local-data/{landing-zone/actuals,landing-zone/employees, #           landing-zone/hierarchies,archive,error} # 5. Bootstrap the database and load seed data make db-bootstrap make db-seed** |
| --- |

## 8.2 Starting the Backend API

Open a terminal, activate the virtual environment, and run:

| **source .venv/bin/activate make api # or directly: uvicorn backend.app.main:app --reload --port 8000 # API is available at: http://localhost:8000 # Interactive docs at: http://localhost:8000/docs  (Swagger UI) # Health check:        http://localhost:8000/health** |
| --- |

## 8.3 Starting the Frontend Dev Server

Open a second terminal and run:

| **cd frontend npm run dev # SPA is available at: http://localhost:5173 # API calls to /api/* are proxied to http://localhost:8000** |
| --- |

## 8.4 Vite Proxy Configuration

The vite.config.ts file proxies all /api/* requests to the local backend, eliminating CORS issues during development:

| **// frontend/vite.config.ts export default defineConfig({   server: {     proxy: {       ****'****/api****'****: {         target: ****'****http://localhost:8000****'****,         changeOrigin: true,       }     }   } })** |
| --- |

## 8.5 Makefile Reference

| **Command** | **Action** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **make api** | Start the FastAPI dev server with --reload | Requires .venv to be activated |
| **make frontend** | Start the Vite frontend dev server |  |
| **make db-bootstrap** | Create all obs.* tables in the local DuckDB file | Idempotent |
| **make db-seed** | Load all seed data in dependency order | Idempotent |
| **make db-reset** | Delete obs.duckdb, re-bootstrap, and re-seed | Destructive — wipes all local data |
| **make dirs** | Create local-data/ directory structure | Safe to run multiple times |
| **make pipeline-actuals FILE=path** | Run the actuals ingestion pipeline against a local file | Drops file into landing-zone and processes it |
| **make pipeline-employees FILE=path** | Run the employee ingestion pipeline against a local file |  |
| **make pipeline-hierarchy FILE=path** | Run the hierarchy ingestion pipeline against a local file |  |
| **make test** | Run all backend tests (pytest) |  |
| **make test-unit** | Run unit tests only |  |
| **make test-integration** | Run integration tests only | Requires a running local API |
| **make lint** | Run ruff (Python) and eslint (TypeScript) |  |
| **make typecheck** | Run mypy (Python) and tsc --noEmit (TypeScript) |  |

# 9. VS Code Debug Configurations

The .vscode/launch.json file provides the following debug configurations. Select them from the VS Code Run and Debug panel (Cmd+Shift+D).

| **Configuration Name** | **What It Launches** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **OBS: FastAPI (Backend)** | uvicorn with --reload, attached to VS Code debugger | Set breakpoints in any backend Python file. The --reload flag is disabled when the debugger is attached to avoid process restart conflicts. |
| **OBS: Pytest (All Tests)** | pytest for all tests in backend/tests/ | Run from VS Code without opening a terminal. |
| **OBS: Pytest (Current File)** | pytest for the currently open test file | Useful for focused test runs during development. |
| **OBS: Pipeline — Actuals** | actuals_pipeline.py with a sample fixture file as input | Runs the actuals ingestion pipeline in debug mode against the fixture in backend/tests/fixtures/. |
| **OBS: Pipeline — Employees** | employees_pipeline.py with a sample fixture file as input |  |
| **OBS: Pipeline — Hierarchy** | hierarchy_pipeline.py with a sample fixture file as input |  |

The frontend (React/TypeScript) is debugged directly in Chrome or Edge using the browser's built-in DevTools. Source maps are enabled by Vite in development mode. No separate VS Code launch configuration is required for the frontend.

# 10. Local Testing Strategy

Three testing layers are defined. All three must pass before any phase is considered complete.

## 10.1 Unit Tests (backend/tests/unit/)

Unit tests cover individual functions and classes in isolation. External dependencies (database, filesystem, notification service) are mocked using pytest fixtures and Python's unittest.mock. Unit tests must run without any running services — no local API, no DuckDB file required.

Coverage targets per module:

- Calculation service (calculation_service.py): 100% line coverage. Every compensation calculation rule, proration logic, merit increase application, burden rate, and AIPEIP bonus rule must have a dedicated unit test.

- Ingestion pipeline validation rules: 100% line coverage of all structural and referential integrity validation logic.

- Auth middleware: 100% line coverage of the mock bypass path and the token validation path (token validation mocked).

- All other service modules: minimum 80% line coverage.

| **# Run all unit tests make test-unit # or: pytest backend/tests/unit/ -v # Run with coverage report pytest backend/tests/unit/ --cov=backend/app --cov-report=term-missing** |
| --- |

## 10.2 Integration Tests (backend/tests/integration/)

Integration tests exercise the full API request/response cycle against a live local backend and local DuckDB database. Each test starts from a known database state (via fixtures that reset and re-seed the database), makes real HTTP requests to the running API using the httpx test client, and asserts on the HTTP response and the resulting database state.

Integration tests cover:

- Every API endpoint: correct HTTP status codes for valid requests; correct 401/403/404/409/422 responses for invalid requests.

- Authorization enforcement: capability flag checks, cost center grant checks, confidential data field exclusion — verified for each relevant endpoint using each test user identity (Section 6.3).

- Audit log writes: every mutation operation generates the correct audit event with the correct fields — verified by querying obs.audit_log after the API call.

- Calculation correctness: end-to-end calculation results verified at the API response level (not just unit-tested in isolation).

- Ingestion pipeline: pipeline scripts invoked against fixture CSV/Excel files; resulting obs.* table state asserted.

| **# Integration tests require the local API to be running # Terminal 1: make api # Terminal 2: make test-integration # or: pytest backend/tests/integration/ -v** |
| --- |

| **Note: ****Integration tests use a separate DuckDB file (local-data/obs-test.duckdb) that is bootstrapped and seeded fresh for each test session. The development database (local-data/obs.duckdb) is never modified by test runs.** |
| --- |

## 10.3 Frontend-Only Testing (API Mocked)

The frontend can be run against a fully mocked API using MSW (Mock Service Worker). This allows frontend development and testing to proceed independently of backend completeness, and allows UI acceptance criteria to be verified without a running backend.

MSW intercepts all /api/* requests in the browser and returns pre-defined mock responses defined in frontend/src/mocks/handlers.ts. MSW is activated by setting VITE_API_MOCK=true in frontend/.env.local.

| **# frontend/.env.local VITE_API_MOCK=true # Then start the frontend as normal cd frontend ****&****&**** npm run dev # All API calls are intercepted by MSW — no backend required** |
| --- |

MSW mock handlers must be kept in sync with the API contract. For each API endpoint defined in the specifications, a corresponding MSW handler must exist. Mock responses must use realistic data matching the obs.* schemas.

## 10.4 Acceptance Criteria Verification

Every AC-* identifier from the specifications must be mapped to a test. The mapping is maintained in a test registry file (backend/tests/ac_registry.yaml) that lists each AC-* identifier, the test file, and the test function that covers it. Claude Code must update this file as tests are written.

| **# backend/tests/ac_registry.yaml (excerpt) AC-CAP-01:   file: integration/test_auth.py   test: test_administrator_has_full_access AC-CAP-02:   file: integration/test_auth.py   test: test_non_admin_cannot_grant_admin_flag # ...** |
| --- |

| **# Verify all AC-***** identifiers have a registered test make ac-coverage # Exits non-zero if any AC-***** identifier is unmapped** |
| --- |

# 11. Testing the Ingestion Pipeline Locally

The ingestion pipeline scripts run as plain Python — no Azure Functions runtime is required locally. The landing zone path and database path are controlled by environment variables.

## 11.1 Using Fixture Files

Sample CSV and Excel fixture files are provided in backend/tests/fixtures/. These files conform exactly to the file format contracts in the Data Integration Specification v1.6 and cover the following cases:

- Valid actuals file: correct structure, all required fields, USD currency, all cost centers and accounts matching seed data.

- Actuals file with quarantine cases: rows with unknown cost center codes, unknown account codes, non-USD currency records.

- Actuals file with high error rate: more than 80% invalid rows — causes file-level rejection.

- Valid employee file: correct structure, all required fields, salary_structure values covering AIPEIP-eligible and ineligible cases.

- Valid cost center hierarchy file: three-level hierarchy matching the seed cost centers.

- Valid account hierarchy file: leaf-level accounts with is_personnel_expense flags set.

- Duplicate file: same content as a previously processed file — verifies idempotency.

## 11.2 Dropping Files into the Landing Zone

| **# Process an actuals fixture file make pipeline-actuals FILE=backend/tests/fixtures/actuals_valid.csv # This copies the file to local-data/landing-zone/actuals/ # and immediately runs actuals_pipeline.py against it. # Verify the result # Open obs.duckdb in VS Code with the DuckDB extension and query: # SELECT COUNT(*****) FROM obs.actuals; # SELECT ***** FROM obs.ingestion_control ORDER BY processed_at DESC LIMIT 5; # SELECT * FROM obs.quarantine ORDER BY quarantined_at DESC LIMIT 10;** |
| --- |

# 12. Switching Between Test Users During Development

To test the application as a different user, update LOCAL_AUTH_USER_ID in .env.local and restart the backend API. The frontend session context will reflect the new user on the next page load.

| **# .env.local — switch to Finance Reviewer LOCAL_AUTH_USER_ID=dev-finance-001 LOCAL_AUTH_USER_EMAIL=finance@obs.local LOCAL_AUTH_USER_NAME=Local Finance Reviewer # Then restart the backend make api** |
| --- |

| **Note: ****Changing the test user does not require a database reset. The user records and their grants are already present in the seed data. Only the backend restart is needed.** |
| --- |

# 13. Impact on Build Sequencing Plan v1.0

The following addition applies to the Build Sequencing Plan v1.0. No existing phase is changed — this specification adds a prerequisite gate that applies before Phase 0 begins.

| **Phase 0 Prerequisite Gate — Local Environment Verified**** Before Phase 0 work begins, the developer must verify the local environment is fully operational: make dirs, make db-bootstrap, and make db-seed complete without errors. make api starts the FastAPI server and GET /health returns HTTP 200. npm run dev starts the Vite frontend without errors. The browser at http://localhost:5173 loads the application shell without authentication errors. make test-unit passes with zero failures.** |
